# Deploy to the homeserver

After changing RBWiki code, deploy it before finishing. The user expects every code change on the homeserver, not only on localhost.

Run from the repo root:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\deploy.ps1
```

- Leave server notes, uploads, and the password in place. Do not pass `-IncludeData` unless the user explicitly asks to replace that data.
- The script updates code on 192.168.31.11 and restarts it with `saferun restart rbwiki`. It does not use the old screen session. It checks `http://127.0.0.1:3010/rbWiki` for 200.
- Do not commit or push git unless the user asks.
- Skip the deploy when the turn did not change app code.
